{"causes": ["The Dutch Republic's rapid rise as a global maritime and commercial power necessitated securing new trade routes and markets in the East.", "The Ottoman Empire's strategic location and control over lucrative trade networks made it an indispensable partner for European mercantile states.", "The existing Capitulations granted to France and England by the Ottoman Porte created a precedent and a competitive pressure for other European powers to seek similar privileges."], "effects": ["The establishment of permanent diplomatic relations between the Dutch Republic and the Ottoman Empire profoundly influenced European diplomacy.", "Dutch merchants gained significant economic advantages and expanded their trade networks throughout the Levant and beyond.", "The Capitulations of 1612 provided a legal framework that secured the rights and privileges of Dutch citizens within Ottoman territories for centuries."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "dutch-republic", "sourceName": "Dutch Republic", "verb": "CREATES", "targetSlug": "cornelius-haga", "targetName": "Cornelius Haga", "context": "The Dutch Republic appointed Cornelius Haga as its first ambassador to the Ottoman Empire in 1612 to secure trade interests."}, {"sourceSlug": "cornelius-haga", "sourceName": "Cornelius Haga", "verb": "CREATES", "targetSlug": "dutch-ottoman-capitulations-1612", "targetName": "Dutch-Ottoman Capitulations of 1612", "context": "Cornelius Haga negotiated the crucial Capitulations of 1612, granting significant trade and legal privileges to Dutch merchants in the Ottoman Empire."}, {"sourceSlug": "ottoman-empire", "sourceName": "Ottoman Empire", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "cornelius-haga", "targetName": "Cornelius Haga", "context": "Cornelius Haga conducted his extensive diplomatic mission primarily within the Ottoman Empire, serving as ambassador in Constantinople for 27 years."}, {"sourceSlug": "cornelius-haga", "sourceName": "Cornelius Haga", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug":